<title>USA: U.S. May personal income rose 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. May personal income rose 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    May    Apr--(Prev)   Mar--(Prev)   Feb</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.3    0.2    0.1    0.6    0.6    0.7</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.3    0.2    0.1    0.5    0.5    0.6</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.3    0.1   Unch    0.4    0.5    0.3</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.3    0.1    0.1    0.2    0.2    0.2</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.4    Unch  Unch    0.1    0.2   -0.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  May     Apr--(Prev)   Mar--(Prev)   Feb</p>
<p> Income		   6,774  6,754  6,753  6,739  6,746  6,701</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,836  5,821  5,820  5,810  5,815  5,781</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,539  5,522  5,524  5,515  5,519  5,505</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,368  5,352  5,355  5,345  5,350  5,335</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   645    644    646    655    656    659</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,583  1,585  1,595  1,596  1,599  1,595  -Services		3,139  3,123  3,114  3,095  3,095  3,081</p>
<p> Personal Savings	 298    298    295    295    296    276</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.1    5.1    5.1    5.1    5.1    4.8</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  May     Apr--(Prev)   Mar--(Prev)   Feb</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,838  3,828  3,825  3,825  3,828  3,797</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   700    700    700    698    699    693</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,357  1,353  1,352  1,352  1,353  1,341</p>
<p> -Government		658    658    659    658    658    656</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    554    553    552    552    551    550</p>
<p> -Farm			 46     46     45     46     45     46</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  508    507    506    506    505    504</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected personal income for May to rise 0.4 percent and spending to increase 0.3 percent.</p>
